106
00:05:23.182 --> 00:05:24.569
Estimation highlights:

107
00:05:24.849 --> 00:05:33.275
Game server capacity: one process runs one BR match of 100 players at 30 Hz, using about 1 to 2 cores.

108
00:05:33.555 --> 00:05:41.043
3M CCU in BR gives 30k matches, which is roughly 30k, 60k cores worldwide at peak.

109
00:05:41.323 --> 00:05:45.547
That fleet has to be elastic, and it is the biggest infrastructure cost.

110
00:05:45.827 --> 00:05:47.129
Bandwidth per player:

111
00:05:47.409 --> 00:05:58.054
30 snapshots per second times ~500 bytes (after delta compression) is ~15 KB per second, or 120 kbps down.

112
00:05:59.404 --> 00:06:05.100
3M players need ~360 Gbps of egress from game servers.

113
00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.239
Egress from game servers is a real cost item.

114
00:06:08.519 --> 00:06:09.564
Match results:

115
00:06:09.844 --> 00:06:15.668
30k matches ending every ~25 minutes is ~20 results per second.

116
00:06:15.948 --> 00:06:24.161
Each result updates up to 100 players, so ~2k leaderboard updates per second on average and more at the top of the hour.

117
00:06:24.441 --> 00:06:25.465
Matchmaking:

118
00:06:25.745 --> 00:06:32.700
3M players cycling every ~25 minutes means ~2k players per second entering queues.

119
