173
00:09:09.271 --> 00:09:11.041
Decision, and Choice, and Why.

174
00:09:11.321 --> 00:09:12.473
Game topology.

175
00:09:12.753 --> 00:09:13.585
Choice:

176
00:09:13.865 --> 00:09:16.873
Dedicated authoritative servers (not peer-to-peer).

177
00:09:17.153 --> 00:09:17.836
Why:

178
00:09:18.116 --> 00:09:21.188
Cheating resistance, fairness, no host advantage.

179
00:09:21.468 --> 00:09:22.407
Transport.

180
00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:23.519
Choice:

181
00:09:23.799 --> 00:09:28.172
UDP with a custom reliability layer (or QUIC or ENet-style).

182
00:09:28.452 --> 00:09:29.135
Why:

183
00:09:29.415 --> 00:09:32.209
TCP head-of-line blocking hurts real time.

184
00:09:32.489 --> 00:09:33.257
Fleet.

185
00:09:33.537 --> 00:09:34.369
Choice:

186
00:09:34.649 --> 00:09:42.713
Container-based fleet management (for example, Kubernetes + Agones, or managed services) across clouds and bare metal.

187
00:09:42.993 --> 00:09:43.676
Why:

188
00:09:43.956 --> 00:09:46.665
Elasticity plus low latency near players.

189
00:09:46.945 --> 00:09:47.969
Matchmaking.

190
00:09:48.249 --> 00:09:49.081
Choice:

191
